        "original_id": "9947d648-7a09-54c8-b556-15b21e570f58",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Wain, Ödön von Horváth\n- Works: Young Shoulders, Tales from the Vienna Woods\n- Organizations: The Movement\n- Roles: poet, novelist, critic, playwright\n\nFacts:\n- Ödön von Horváth was born as Edmund Josef von Horváth on 9 December 1901 in Sušak, Rijeka, then in Austria–Hungary and now in Croatia.\n- Tales from the Vienna Woods is a 1931 play by Ödön von Horváth and is described as his most famous play.\n- Ödön von Horváth was a German-writing playwright and novelist of Austro-Hungarian birth, and he died in Paris on 1 June 1938.\n- John Barrington Wain was born on 14 March 1925 and was an English poet, novelist, and critic associated with the literary group The Movement.\n- Young Shoulders is a 1982 novel by John Wain.\n- John Wain was appointed CBE and died on 24 May 1994.",
